Package: potion
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: IP flow monitor
 Potion is a console utility that listens on a network interface using
 libpcap, aggregates the traffic it sees into flows, and displays the
 busiest of them with their average throughput, as many as fit on the
 screen. The display refreshes once a second and is sorted by rate.
 .
 A flow is identified by the IP protocol, the type of service field, the
 source and destination addresses, and the source and destination ports.
 Fragmented datagrams are reassembled into the flow they belong to once
 the fragment carrying the port numbers has been seen.
 .
 Capturing needs privileges, so potion is normally started through sudo.
 It gives them up as soon as the capture handle is open, and runs the
 rest of the session as the invoking user.
